an #if expands a macro until it is a number, not once.

A MACRO WHOSE BODY IS ANOTHER MACRO NAME EVALUATED TO ZERO in a preprocessor
conditional:

    #define SHT_RELA 4
    #define SHT_RELX SHT_RELA
    #if SHT_RELX == SHT_RELA        FALSE -- strtoint("SHT_RELA") is 0

macro_variable looked the name up once and handed the expansion token straight
to strtoint. One level was enough for almost everything, which is why it
survived: `SHT_RELA == 4` was always right, and `SHT_RELY == SHT_RELX` compared
two unexpanded names and matched by accident.

WHAT IT COST, AND IT IS NOT A CODEGEN BUG -- IT DELETED A LINE OF tcc.
tcc.h has exactly that pair:

    # define SHT_RELX SHT_RELA

and tccelf.c guards the addend store with it:

    #if SHT_RELX == SHT_RELA
        rel->r_addend = addend;
    #endif

So mc-tcc compiled OUT the line that writes a relocation's addend. Every static
initialiser of the form `pointer = array + N` lost its offset:

    static const int32_t *const ptable = table + 128;      musl, __ctype_b_loc.c

    control:  R_AARCH64_ABS64   table + 200
    mc-tcc:   R_AARCH64_ABS64   table + 0

The pointer aimed at element 0. Silent, systematic, and it survived the
gen2 == gen3 == gen4 fixpoint untouched -- a fixpoint proves a compiler is
STABLE, not correct.

THE RUNTIME GUARD ON THE NEXT LINE NEVER FIRED, and that is the tell:

    if (SHT_RELX != SHT_RELA && addend)
        tcc_error_noabort("non-zero addend on REL architecture");

The compiled code agreed the two were equal. Only the preprocessor did not.

HOW IT WAS FOUND, because the method is the transferable part. Not by reading
tcc, and not by any of the case suites -- they were all green. A gcc-built
CONTROL tcc was built from the same source, both compilers were run over
musl's 1312 sources, and the object files were compared with `cmp`. 244 of the
first 250 were byte-identical; one of the six differed by a single byte, in
`.rela.data.ro`, and that byte was the addend. From there it was three
instrumented rebuilds to the `#if`.

BOUNDED, because a macro may name itself. M2-Planet's blue paint covers
expansion in the body of the program; this is a separate evaluator with its own
walk, so it carries its own limit rather than borrowing that one.

MEASURED, EITHER SIDE:

    the reduced case          #if SHT_RELX == SHT_RELA   FALSE -> TRUE
    ctype addend              table + 0 -> table + 200, matching the control
    musl object diff          1175 identical, 131 differ, 0 subject-only
                              failures -- and 128 of the 131 are src/math,
                              the other three are floatscan, vfprintf and
                              getloadavg. EVERY REMAINING DIVERGENCE IS
                              FLOATING POINT.
    difftest amd64            108 pass, 0 fail
    difftest aarch64          110 pass, 0 fail
    stage 2 corpus            420 of 426
    mc-tcc                    builds, twelve.sh 12 of 12

That last measurement is the one worth keeping: with this patch in, mc-tcc's
INTEGER codegen is byte-identical to a gcc-built tcc across 1175 real objects.

--- a/cc_macro.c
+++ b/cc_macro.c
@@ -303,11 +303,46 @@
 }
 
